    <DataNode elementId="AT5G12200-MONOMER" textLabel="dihydropyrimidinase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT5G12200-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="295" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">PYD2 from Arabidopsis can complement a pyd2 mutant in &lt;i&gt;Saccharomyces kluyveri&lt;/i&gt; indicating that it has dihydropyrimidinase activity |CITS: [12626710]|. In addition, mutant analyses indicate the importance of this enzyme for uracil catabolism in |FRAME: ORG-5993 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; col| |CITS: [19413687]|. Mutants that lack a full-length functional copy of this gene have higher levels of uracil and decreased levels of CO&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; production from C14-labeled uracil. In addition, &lt;i&gt;pyd2&lt;/i&gt; mutant plants cannot survive on uracil as their sole nitrogen source |CITS: [19413687]| suggesting that this enzyme is required for uracil catabolism in |FRAME: ORG-5993 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; col|. A PYD2-GFP fusion localizes to the secretory system in transformed Arabidopsis mesophyll cells |CITS: [19413687]|. Based on analyses of similar proteins from other species, it is likely that this enzyme functions in thymine degradation (reductive) and can also catalyze the addition of water to |FRAME: DIHYDRO-THYMINE 5,6-dihydrothymine|, leading to the production of |FRAME: 3-UREIDO-ISOBUTYRATE 3-ureido-isobutyrate| |CITS: [19413687]|, but, this has not been verified &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; or &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt;.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G12200-MONOMER" />
